      "id": "process_gases_precursors",
      "set": {},
      "append_notes": " Episode context (neon_gas_lithography_supply_shock, 2022): Ukraine's three major neon suppliers—Ingas, Cryoin, and Iceblick—collectively provided 45-70% of semiconductor-grade neon globally. Russian invasion (Feb 2022) halted Ukrainian production for 6-12 months, creating acute shortages at TSMC, Samsung, Intel. Crisis resolved by H2 2023-2024 through diversification to US (Matheson), Japan, and reduced demand normalization. Not flagged as current bottleneck (2026) as supply diversified post-crisis, though concentration in gas supply remains a latent risk."
    },
    {
      "id": "foundry_capacity_tsmc",
      "append_evidenceIds": [
        "ev_acc_logic2_tsmc_foundry_capacity_updated"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "logic_die_fabrication",
      "append_evidenceIds": [
        "ev_acc_logic2_tsmc_foundry_capacity_updated"
      ],
      "append_notes": " N3/N5 allocation episode (leading_edge_foundry_capacity_n3_n5, 2023-2026): TSMC's 3nm capacity has remained near-full utilization (>95%) through 2025-2026 due to sustained AI accelerator demand. TSMC allocates production among customers (NVIDIA, AMD, custom silicon) with multi-quarter lead times and contracted volumes. Samsung Foundry emerged as secondary source (8-12% market share, 12 KWPM 3nm-equivalent capacity) but faces qualification and yield challenges vs TSMC. Current (Q2 2026) constraint remains TSMC 3nm utilization and foundry lead times; no relief expected until 2027."
    },
    {
      "id": "euv_photomask_production",
      "append_evidenceIds": [
        "ev_acc_logic2_euv_mask_duopoly"
      ]
    }
  ],
